    {
      "id": "claim_a05bba7cf5f54e1d902514bb1447f59c",
      "statement": "At 2025-12-31 total asset dollar duration is about +28.5bn and total liability dollar duration about -27.1bn per 100 bp, giving a net +1,368.7 and an EVE change of +2,737.40 (+2.47% of Tier 1) at -200 bp, +1,368.70 at -100 bp, -1,368.70 at +100 bp, and -2,737.40 (-2.47%) at +200 bp. The firm is value-exposed to rising rates because the duration of mortgages and securities exceeds that of modeled deposit liabilities, opposite to its asset-sensitive NII position.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/models/nii-sensitivity-model.md#L410-L430",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c144852d627892a2fd4e6424dd7781a7179ee1ac6ee01287f2b24ba6d512f100:"
