    {
      "id": "claim_5f1caa017b494ca59404e2ca8ebe6ad6",
      "statement": "Behavioral deposit durations are key judgment inputs: noninterest-bearing deposits are assigned 3.5 years and consumer interest-bearing deposits 2.8 years, which together contribute about -20.8bn of liability dollar duration per 100 bp and offset most of the asset-side duration, so the net EVE result is a small difference between two large figures. The EVE sheet has no in-sheet validation check on durations or balances.",
